{"id":"chatcmpl-00db524c-c3ff-4fa7-bba9-ec855b6ef7ad","object":"chat.completion","created":1795251794,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation: querying multiple independent expert tools with the same clinical question and requiring convergent evidence before committing to an answer. The key insight is that laterality determination on lateral views is error-prone, so independent confirmation from a second model increases confidence. The pattern generalizes to any ambiguous visual classification task where a single model's judgment may be unreliable.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a visual finding requires determining laterality or spatial orientation that is ambiguous on a single view, query multiple independent expert models with the same targeted question and require agreement before answering.\",\n    \"Decompose the diagnostic question into a specific anatomical criterion (e.g., 'posterior costophrenic angle blunting') rather than asking broadly, so each expert tool produces a focused, checkable judgment.\",\n    \"Use cross-validation across heterogeneous tools (specialized expert + general VLM) to reduce single-model bias when the answer hinges on subtle visual evidence.\",\n    \"When multiple independent sources converge on the same finding, commit to the answer with a reason that explicitly cites the convergent evidence from each source.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical image QA\": \"Ask each expert tool a narrowly scoped anatomical question (specific landmark + specific abnormality) rather than the full multiple-choice question; then reconcile answers.\",\n    \"Ambiguous visual classification\": \"Identify the single most error-prone dimension (here: laterality) and target redundant queries specifically at that dimension.\",\n    \"Multi-tool consensus\": \"Prefer agreement between a domain-specialist tool and a general-purpose model over repeated queries to the same tool.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm that each expert tool was asked the same focused clinical question so their answers are directly comparable.\",\n    \"Verify the final answer's rationale explicitly references the convergent findings from each independent source.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":507,"total_tokens":899,"completion_tokens":392,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":507},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":392}}}